{"person_id":"candidate-1912-jay-leno","name":"Jay Leno","cohort_group":"Creators / artists","category":"Comedian / television host","birth_year":1950,"age_at_milestone":26,"milestone_by_age_26":"Made his first appearance on The Tonight Show with Johnny Carson on March 2, 1977, performing a stand-up comedy routine on the premier late-night platform for comedians.","early_history_summary":"Leno grew up in Andover, Massachusetts, and discovered comedy in high school, encouraged by a teacher who let him give a talk instead of writing a paper. He made his professional debut at the Nameless Coffeehouse in Harvard Square in 1969 at age 19, started a comedy club at Emerson College in 1973, and moved to Los Angeles in 1974 to work the comedy club circuit before landing his first Tonight Show spot at 26.","primary_leverage_engine":"Relentless work ethic","normalized_primary_engine":"Execution / operations","secondary_engine":"Direct audience reps","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":1,"prior_reps_score":2,"scarce_skill_depth_score":1,"native_distribution_score":0,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":1,"complementary_team_score":0,"structural_wave_score":1,"concentration_intensity_score":2,"capital_safety_score":0,"domain_proximity_score":2,"total_leverage_score":10,"success_tier":2,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","family_context_summary":"Born to a middle-class family in New Rochelle, NY; father was an Italian-American insurance salesman, mother a Scottish-born homemaker who immigrated to the US at age 11. Grew up in Andover, Massachusetts.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Not documented in reviewed sources; no entertainment industry connections in the family.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":0,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":0,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":0,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":0,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":1,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":0,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":0,"exceptiona